<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Abiove sees soy crop at 26.5-27.5 mln tns.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Abiove sees soy crop at 26.5-27.5 mln tns.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's soybean crop should come in between 26.5 and 27.5 million tonnes, the Brazilian Association of Vegetable Oils Industries (Abiove) said, upping its previous forecast of 26 to 27 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The upward revision was because of this year's high productivity levels, it said, adding that the new crop forecast compared with a revised 23.9 million tonne output in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Exports should rise sharply to between 6.5 and 7.5 million tonnes against 3.6 million tonnes in 1996/97, Abiove said.</p>
<p>&quot;Exports...should reach a record $5.2 billion, registering an increase of more than $700 million in 1997,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Abiove estimates imports of soybeans at 1.5 million tonnes in the coming year against a downwardly revised 1.1 million tonnes in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Imports of soymeal should also grow slightly to 200,000 tonnes from last year's 100,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Supply and demand estimates for 1997/98 and 1996/97 follow.</p>
<p>All figures are in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p> SOYBEANS		 1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    550	     850</p>
<p> Production	 26,500 to 27,500  23,950</p>
<p> Imports		   1,500	   1,100</p>
<p> Seeds and losses	1,600	   1,600</p>
<p> Exports	     6,500 to 7,500    3,650</p>
<p> Crushings		19,800	  20,100</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    650	     550</p>
<p> SOYMEAL		  1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    347	     547</p>
<p> Production	     15,700	  15,900</p>
<p> Imports		     200	     100</p>
<p> Internal demand	 5,600	   5,300</p>
<p> Exports		  10,300	  10,900</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    347	     347</p>
<p> SOYOIL		   1997/98	 1996/97</p>
<p> Opening stocks	    195	     195</p>
<p> Production		3,750	   3,800</p>
<p> Imports		     200	     200</p>
<p> Internal demand	 2,750	   2,650</p>
<p> Exports		   1,200	   1,350</p>
<p> Closing stocks	    195	     195</p>
